    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c98ce8ec-d054-5b9e-a46c-bb09f63f357f",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(\\theta+\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin \\theta$ and $\\cos \\theta$. Enter the signed coefficients.\n\n$\\cos\\left(\\theta+\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)=$ {{field-1}} $\\sin \\theta\\,+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos \\theta$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=\\theta$ and $v=\\frac{5\\pi}{3}$, the exact values are $\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(\\theta+\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)&=\\cos \\theta\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)-\\sin \\theta\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos \\theta\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\sin \\theta\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin \\theta+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos \\theta.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
